A||N||2||mbramble||Oil Filter Question||||1||
Z||000000||mbramble||05-25-2000||08:10 AM||||What is the correct oil filter for an '87 2.5L????<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||05-25-2000||10:51 AM||||ACDelco PF 47 (short body) or PF 52 (Long body). long body is both easier to install and is a bigger filter.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||05-25-2000||11:45 AM||||Thanks Ogre.  The car had a long body filter on it the first time I changed oil.  But the cross reference books at the parts store don't show PF52 as an option, so I ended up with the short one.  My dipstick says PF51 but I can't find one of those. And the ACDelco only shows PF47 for both 2.8L and 2.5L.  <P>I'll pick up a PF52 on the way home!||||reg||1
